ventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO ATSUNOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKATSUCHI MASAHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WADA HIROMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YONEMOTO YOSHIFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CHIBA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIROSE, TAKAKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, ATSUNOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKATSUCHI, MASAHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WADA, HIROMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YONEMOTO, YOSHIFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A mobile terminal having relatively small data memory, such as a cellular phone, is provided which never fails to receive PUSH messages sent irregularly from an information provider. Message request means (104) checks for free space in message storage means (103) based on the contents of a notification received by transmitter/receiver means (101), and requests the acquisition of the message from a Web protocol processing means (102) if sufficient memory is available. Message analysis means (105) analyzes the message returned from a server. Message management means (106) stores the analyzed message in the message storing means (103). When asked, the message management means checks for free space in the message storage means (103) and informs the message request means (104) of whether free space is available or not.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un terminal mobile possédant une mémoire de données relativement petite, tel un téléphone cellulaire, qui reçoit sans faute des messages PUSH envoyés irrégulièrement par un fournisseur d'informations. Un dispositif de demande de message (104) vérifie l'espace libre disponible dans la mémoire de messages (103) sur la base du contenu d'une notification reçue par un dispositif d'émission/ réception (101), et demande l'acquisition du message à partir d'un moyen de traitement de protocole Web (102) si la mémoire disponible est suffisante. Un moyen d'analyse de message (105) analyse le message retourné par un serveur. Un moyen de gestion de messages (106) stocke le message analysé dans une mémoire de messages (103). Sur demande, le moyen de gestion de messages vérifie l'espace libre dans la mémoire de messages (103) et informe le dispositif de demande de message (104) de la présence ou non d'espace libre disponible.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>